<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in October.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) announced on Friday the buffer stock sales planned for October would total a maximum 4,251 tonnes and would comprise the following cocoa, the ICCO said.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale are as follows.</p>
<p> TONNES   ORIGIN	     PORT	 CROP	  QUALITY</p>
<p> 118	Ivory Coast	Amsterdam  1981/82     good fermented</p>
<p> 49	 Ivory Coast	Amsterdam  1982/83     good fermented</p>
<p> 50	 Ivory Coast	Antwerp    1981/82     good fermented</p>
<p> 1,208    Ivory Coast	Antwerp    1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p> 301	Ivory Coast	Antwerp    1987/88     fair fermented</p>
<p> 50	 Ivory Coast	Rotterdam  1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p> 25	 Togo		 Rotterdam  1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p> 600	Ghana		Antwerp    1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p> 591	Ghana		Antwerp    1987/88     fair fermented</p>
<p> 248	Nigeria	    Antwerp    1986/87     good fermented</p>
<p> 207	Nigeria	    Antwerp    1986/87     fair fermented</p>
<p> TONNES   ORIGIN	  PORT	 CROP     WAREHOUSE   QUALITY</p>
<p>							  KEEPER</p>
<p> 401	Ivory Coast   Amsterdam  1981/82  Ocean	  FAQ</p>
<p>							  Warehousing</p>
<p> 197	Ivory Coast   Amsterdam  1982/83  Nedveem	FAQ</p>
<p> 125	Ivory Coast   Rotterdam  1981/82  Ocean	  FAQ</p>
<p> 81	 Nigeria	 Rotterdam  1986/87  Ocean	  FAQ</p>
<p>(FAQ=fair average quality)</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London Newsroom 044 71 542 4985</p>
